-- title:
--   Quotient of a norm-one torus Hopf algebra by a power pair
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $c \in K$. Let $B_0$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a $K$-Hopf algebra whose comultiplication is cocommutative, and let $u_0, v_0 \in B_0$ generate $B_0$ as a $K$-algebra (the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\{u_0,v_0\}$ is all of $B_0$) and satisfy the norm-one relation $u_0^2 - c\,v_0^2 = 1$ together with $\Delta(u_0) = u_0 \otimes u_0 + c\,(v_0 \otimes v_0)$ and $\Delta(v_0) = u_0 \otimes v_0 + v_0 \otimes u_0$. Suppose further that $P, Q \in B_0$ satisfy the same shape of data: $P^2 - c\,Q^2 = 1$, $\Delta(P) = P \otimes P + c\,(Q \otimes Q)$, $\Delta(Q) = P \otimes Q + Q \otimes P$, and in addition $\varepsilon(P) = 1$, $\varepsilon(Q) = 0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $A$ with a commutative ring structure and a $K$-Hopf algebra structure whose comultiplication is cocommutative, elements $u', v' \in A$, and a $K$-algebra homomorphism $\pi : B_0 \to A$ such that $\pi(u_0) = u'$, $\pi(v_0) = v'$, $\pi(P) = 1$, $\pi(Q) = 0$; such that every $K$-algebra homomorphism $g : B_0 \to \overline{K}$ into the algebraic closure of $K$ with $g(P) = 1$ and $g(Q) = 0$ factors as $g = f \circ \pi$ for some $K$-algebra homomorphism $f : A \to \overline{K}$; and such that $u', v'$ generate $A$ as a $K$-algebra and satisfy the same relations as $u_0, v_0$, namely $u'^2 - c\,v'^2 = 1$, $\Delta(u') = u' \otimes u' + c\,(v' \otimes v')$ and $\Delta(v') = u' \otimes v' + v' \otimes u'$.
--
--   This is the construction step for passing from a norm-one torus Hopf algebra to its quotient by the Hopf ideal generated by $P-1$ and $Q$, the quotient being again of norm-one torus shape and receiving exactly those $\overline{K}$-points of $B_0$ at which $P=1$ and $Q=0$. It is used by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_powerPair`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_powerPair) in the analysis of finite flat group schemes of norm-one torus type arising in the study of the Galois representations attached to the Frey curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_exists_normOneTorus_hopfIdeal_quotient_of_powerPair.lean

